@misc{gate-F1-absent-and-empty-are-opposite,
  section  = {finding},
  claim    = {ABSENT and EMPTY are OPPOSITE baseline states and were conflated under the single word degraded — ABSENT is a free pass, EMPTY is zero-tolerance.},
  check    = {standing},
  note     = {kind=finding by=gate-oracle. An ABSENT baseline file makes set_ratchet take its no-baseline branch and EXIT 0 WHATEVER IT MEASURED — measured, check_mypy_ratchet --quiet exited 0 while printing would record 116 type errors. An EMPTY baseline reads as the empty set, so every offender is a NEW key: the STRONGEST setting, nothing grandfathered, and never a defect. Operator 2026-08-21: EMPTY is not degraded, EMPTY is no exceptions granted. STANDING. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): ABSENT takes set_ratchet's no-baseline branch and exits 0 whatever it measured; EMPTY is the empty set, so every offender is a NEW key — zero tolerance}
}

