by 'opener=connect tenant=live mode=ro caller=store.py:480' -- the contract-compliant shape, tenant resolving by FLAG and delegating to connect. So the lens fires, names the opener, and distinguishes the resolution path. SECOND, THE ACTUAL TEST: pycodemod --selftest under the same sink emitted exactly ONE row, 'opener=sandbox_connect tenant=sandbox mode=rw label=- caller=_pycodemod_sql.py:860'. No connect row, no live row. (a) IS THEREFORE STALE. gate-F29's fatal pair is both repaired in the tree: _pg_probe_con is now a one-line 'return _pg_sandbox_con()' with the live read-write arm DELETED (its docstring records the three-arm measurement proving the live store contributed nothing a parser needs), and the swallow now records _PG_SANDBOX_ERR with pg_probe_status as the positive control, so 'no store reachable' and 'connected fine' are no longer the same reading. The site still does not consult argv -- but that is now the CORRECT spelling, not a defect: this is gate-F24's require= case, a probe whose tenant is fixed by what it IS (a throwaway parser oracle), not the operator's to pick. A --sandbox pragma would still be a false declaration; 'unstatable' was the right word for a bypass and is the wrong word for a pin. ⚑ SO WHY STILL NO. NOT because the lens is inadequate -- it is decorrelated exactly as specified, total over all three openers (--calls _lens_record: 3 calls, one per opener), unconditional with no opt-out, and it CANNOT MISS AN OPEN BECAUSE IT IS THE OPEN. The blocker MOVED AGAIN and is now purely one of WIRING: run_selftests --tenants HAS NO LENS ARM. Its output today is built from import-closure plus the call-site lens, the two correlated source censuses, and it STILL PRINTS 'pycodemod.py OWED-UNSTATABLE' with gate-F29's full paragraph attached -- a verdict the runtime lens refutes in one row. Minting a --declarations baseline now would freeze a population computed by two instruments while the third, which the refusal itself named as the precondition, sits unread by the census. That is census-green-is-a-fact-about-the-census with the added sting that the disconfirming instrument already exists in-tree. THE REMAINING WORK IS NAMED AND SMALL: give --tenants a lens arm (run each suite with SUBSTRATE_TENANT_LENS set, read the sink back, reconcile against the static population), and the OWED-UNSTATABLE row resolves itself. ⚑ AND MY OWN EDIT THIS ROUND MADE THE CASE FOR IT: sppf_query and reuse_tui now genuinely reach a store, the lens sees them perfectly, and --tenants counts them in NEITHER the declared nor the OWED column -- because they have no selftest, so they are not among the 101 suites at all. The census is scoped to suites; store reach is not. Same two-questions-not-one shape as gate-F28.}
