en I changed the tree this round. The per-row prose did not, because nothing derives it. So the census is simultaneously accurate in every number and wrong in the one paragraph a reader would actually act on — and that paragraph is the reason a --declarations baseline is being withheld (gate-F30). This is cite-a-symbol-never-a-line one level up: the text cites CODE rather than a line, and the code was deleted. ⚑ IT IS ALSO A SECOND INSTANCE OF fresh-comments-are-hypotheses-too: this adjudication was written days ago BY THIS SAME ARC, was correct when written, was inherited by three successive briefs as current, and none of us re-derived it until a runtime instrument existed to contradict it. THE REPAIR IS THE ONE gate-F36 ALREADY NAMES: give --tenants a lens arm, so the verdict is DERIVED from an observed open rather than restated from a reading. Until then the row should at minimum cite pg_probe_status as the check rather than quote a body.}
