(2026-09-26): Ⓐ4b, and it REFUTES the finding it was sent to convert. gate-F-fixture-category says the FIXTURE kind LANDED. The MECHANISM did land -- scratch/toolmodes.py:1480 holds the marker token and _fixtures() at :1484 reads it out of each tool's source. IT HAS ZERO ADOPTERS. Measured 2026-08-24: pycodemod --literal -- toolmodes:fixture scripts/sppf_db.py returns 0 sites, and toolmodes --find --selftest-demo-failure reports it 'dispatched by scripts/sppf_db.py, in no usage line -- UNDOCUMENTED'. So the canonical fixture -- a mode that exists to FAIL, as a positive control proving a selftest harness can report failure at all, which is the exact case the kind was designed for and which gate-F-fixture-category names -- is STILL counted as UNDOCUMENTED debt in the live divergence census. THE OFFERED PAYDOWN IS THEREFORE STILL 'write a usage line', which that finding itself says is worse debt than the row it clears. This is gate-F12-tenant-mechanism-has-zero-adopters recurring one surface over: a mechanism LANDING is not a mechanism ADOPTED, and a finding that says LANDED without naming its adopter count reads as done. THE MEASUREMENT STANDS, established by both arms: pycodemod --literal -- toolmodes:fixture against scripts/sppf_db.py finds 0 sites, and against scratch/toolmodes.py finds 2, so the tool and the search both work and the zero is a fact about sppf_db rather than about the method. ⚑ WHY THIS IS UNWITNESSED RATHER THAN MECHANICAL: the discriminating quantity is a census VALUE (0 sites vs some sites) and every behavioural kind here reads an EXIT CODE. I first registered it as refuses: and the witness immediately reported EXITS 0 -- the refusal is GONE against a finding that is true, because pycodemod --literal exits 0 on a zero result the same as on a hit. Recorded rather than silently re-kinded: it is the census-vs-predicate confusion, one kind over from the documentation-vs-behaviour confusion the selftest: kind was built to end. UNBLOCKED BY: a fifth kind that reads a census value, which should not be built for one finding. NOT A REPAIR I CAN MAKE EITHER: scripts/sppf_db.py is not this agent's file.}
