@misc{meta-F8-pairing-drift-was-unsurfaced-and-cost-a-duplicate,
  section  = {finding},
  claim    = {The witness/bib pairing disagreement was surfaced nowhere despite the registry header claiming --list shows it, the real drift is 34 rows not 4, and the invisibility cost a duplicate finding},
  check    = {selftest:python3,.claude/agents/findings.py,--pairing},
  note     = {kind=finding by=witness-adequacy-write. Ⓐ10, measured 2026-08-24 by the new --pairing mode: 24 witnesses with no bib entry and 10 bib entries with no witness, over 173 witnesses and 159 entries in 6 ledgers. The brief named sql-F34..F37; those were the four a human happened to notice. ROOT: the WITNESSES header says a key with no bib entry is a roster/record disagreement and that --list is where it shows. It is not -- --list prints verdicts and never reads a bib, and register reports the pairing only for the ONE key being filed, so the only way to notice an unpaired witness was to file a NEW one and read its footer. A claim about where a defect surfaces, in the file whose job is surfacing defects, never true. ⚑ THE DRIFT IS INVISIBILITY, NOT UNTIDINESS, MEASURED ON MYSELF: the reuse-search before filing reads the BIBS, so a witness with no entry is absent from it. I re-derived sql-F38 from scratch by a different route and it was already the closing paragraph of sql-F34, whose witness had no bib entry. ⚑⚑ THE 10 BIB-ONLY ROWS ARE NOT A SECOND POPULATION: tmi-F6/F7/F8/F9 exist as bare stems in the witness roster and as descriptive keys in the bib -- one finding, two spellings, counted twice and paired never. census-keyed-on-one-spelling inside the pairing census itself, and a naive paydown would file four duplicate entries and four duplicate witnesses. ⚑ --pairing REPORTS, DOES NOT GATE, because a BIB-ONLY key is often an entry filed seconds before its witness by a concurrent agent; and it REFUSES rather than reporting when bibstruct fails, since an unreadable bib is not an empty one. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): Ⓐ10 bib-roster-drift, and the drift is 34 rows not 4. Measured 2026-08-24 by the new --pairing mode: 24 witnesses with no bib entry and 10 bib entries with no witness, over 173 witnesses and 159 entries in 6 ledgers. THE BRIEF NAMED sql-F34..F37; those were the four a human happened to notice. ROOT: the