BLISHED BY EXECUTION on four independent reverts, not by argument: deleting the _selftest rc-is-None arm gives 49/50, reverting _evidence to tail gives 47/50, reverting _failing_case to tail gives 46/50, and one copy reverting _kinds_rows plus the _restem hyphen plus the polarity probe gives 45/50 naming all five. AND THE FIRST NEGATIVE CONTROL FOUND A DEFECT IN MY OWN SUITE: the rc-is-None revert made the fallthrough format None with percent-d, so the case CRASHED the suite mid-run instead of failing, and every later case went unreported -- one regression hiding the rest, which is the exact defect the sql-F32 negative control found in that suite. Added okf, which records an exception as the case failure text.}
