@misc{meta-F12-selftest-witnesses-cited-the-score-not-the-failure,
  section  = {finding},
  claim    = {the eight selftest witnesses cited tail-of-output, which for the house n/m suite shape is ALWAYS the score and NEVER the failing case -- reliably wrong, not merely unreliable},
  check    = {selftest:python3,.claude/agents/findings.py,--selftest},
  note     = {kind=finding by=witness-adequacy-write. A16. A11 repaired the citation defect on the four refuses witnesses only. All eight selftest witnesses currently PASS, so the failing branch that quotes anything has never been read -- a citation nobody has seen is not one anyone has checked. Verified on three live subjects: ratchet 58/58, store 24/24, findings 50/50, each ending with the score. Repair is _failing_case, a SECOND reader rather than an extension of _evidence, because a FAIL line contains none of the refusal vocabulary and one shared reader would match a union that quotes a refusal word out of a test name. It carries the score alongside, appends the extra-failure count, and reports a score-with-no-FAIL-line as that gap. Evidence chooses the QUOTE and never the verdict. Revert measured: 46/50. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): A16 evidence-line-audit. A11 measured the citation defect on the four refuses witnesses and repaired only those; the eight selftest witnesses print their own tails and were never examined. AUDITED, and they are the harder half. Two findings. FIRST, ALL EIGHT CURRENTLY PASS, so the failing branch is the only one that quotes anything and it has never been READ by anyone -- a citation nobody has seen is not a citation anyone has checked, which is why this class hid behind a green while its dual was being repaired. SECOND, tail-of-output is not merely unreliable here, it is RELIABLY WRONG, and that is a stronger claim than A11 could make about refusals. The house suite shape prints per-case FAIL name colon why lines and THEN a suite colon n slash m score, so the last non-blank line is ALWAYS the arithmetic and NEVER the failure. Verified by running the three live subjects: ratchet.py --selftest ends 58 slash 58, store.py --selftest ends 24 slash 24, findings.py --selftest ends 50 slash 50. An auditor handed the score is told how many failed and never which, and the failing case sits on the lines immediately above where tail cannot look. REPAIR: _failing_case, a SECOND reader rather than an extension of _evidence -- _evidence hunts refusal vocabulary (refus, denied, must) and a FAIL line contains none of it, so sharing one reader would mean matching a union of vocabularies against both shapes, which is how a reader starts quoting a refusal word out of a test name. It quotes the first FAIL line, appends the extra-failure count so later cases are not hidden, and carries the score alongside rather than instead. A score with no FAIL line is reported AS that gap, because a suite exiting non-zero while naming no case is under-instrumented and saying so beats quoting arithmetic. SAME CONTRACT AS A11: it chooses which line to QUOTE and never the verdict; rc not equal 0 decides OPEN before any text is read. DISCRIMINATION BY EXECUTION: reverting _failing_case to the last line gives 46 of 50 on four cases.}
