@misc{meta-F13-register-can-detect-polarity-not-censusness,
  section  = {finding},
  claim    = {register CAN refuse the census-vs-predicate confusion, but by EXECUTING the command at filing time and checking polarity -- no static check exists, and polarity is narrower than census-ness},
  check    = {selftest:python3,.claude/agents/findings.py,--selftest},
  note     = {kind=finding by=witness-adequacy-write. A12. A census reports a VALUE and exits 0 on zero exactly as on a hit, a predicate reports an EXIT CODE, and nothing in the argv text distinguishes them, so a static check is impossible in principle. Execution is free at filing time because the witness runs the command anyway. _probe_polarity refuses a refuses-command exiting 0, a selftest-command exiting non-zero, and a command that cannot start. That is the gate-F38 case caught at the filing site instead of banked. THE BOUNDARY, stated rather than glossed: this detects WRONG POLARITY, not census-ness -- a census whose zero result exited non-zero would still register and still be a category error. What it guarantees is that no witness is born reporting the opposite of the finding it holds. NO FIFTH KIND, per gate-F14. The refusal names both causes rather than asserting one. Revert measured: 45/50. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): A12 census-vs-predicate. THE ANSWER IS YES BUT NARROWER THAN THE QUESTION, and stating the boundary is the finding. A CENSUS reports a VALUE and exits 0 on a zero result exactly as on a hit; a PREDICATE reports an EXIT CODE. Nothing in a command TEXT distinguishes them -- pycodemod --literal -- toolmodes:fixture scripts/sppf_db.py and schema.py --cancel 99999999 are the same argv shape -- so a STATIC check is impossible in principle and no amount of parsing recovers it. WHAT IS AVAILABLE IS EXECUTION, AND IT IS FREE AT FILING TIME. The witness will run this command on every --list; running it ONCE MORE at registration answers the only question that matters, which is whether it exits the way the kind requires TODAY. _probe_polarity does that: a refuses command exiting 0 is refused at the point of filing, a selftest command exiting non-zero is refused, and a command that cannot start at all is refused rather than filed as mechanical while reporting 2 forever. That is exactly the gate-F38 case -- --literal returned 0 sites with exit 0 and the freshly filed witness immediately reported the refusal is GONE against a finding that was perfectly true. It is now caught at the filing site instead of banked for the next reader. THE HONEST BOUNDARY: this detects WRONG POLARITY, not census-ness. A census whose zero result happened to exit non-zero would still register as refuses and would still be a category error, and the probe cannot see it. What it guarantees is that no witness is ever born reporting the opposite of the finding it was filed to hold, which is the shape that actually cost a false verdict here. NO FIFTH KIND WAS BUILT, per gate-F14 and per gate-F38 own note. The refusal names BOTH causes rather than asserting one: either the refusal genuinely is not installed, so the finding is OPEN and refuses is right but premature, or this is a census and its honest kind is unwitnessed. DISCRIMINATION BY EXECUTION: removing the probe from the refuses branch gives 45 of 50 with the two polarity cases red; and the two correct-polarity acceptance cases guard against the probe becoming a wall rather than a gate.}
}

@misc{meta-F14-pairing-census-was-keyed-on-one-spelling,
