o unrelated findings marry, which is the ambiguity resolve already refuses rather than guesses. TRUE DRIFT IS 26 ROWS, NOT 30: 16 witness-only, 6 bib-only, 4 spelling pairs to RE-KEY rather than file. Both counts are printed so a reader can see the reduction rather than trust it. AND THE UNPAIRED-ON-BOTH-SIDES CONDITION IS NOT DECORATION. proc-F1 and proc-F2 are bib-only and the roster holds proc-F1-cpu-floor-cannot-see-abandonment and proc-F2-times-is-not-a-read, but those witnesses have their own bib entries and are about different subjects. A prefix match against a PAIRED key is stem REUSE (swarm-F3-key-allocation-has-no-detector), not a spelling, and marrying them would have produced two false pairs on the live roster. Measured: they correctly stay BIB-ONLY. AMBIGUITY IS REPORTED, NOT RESOLVED: one stem prefixing several unpaired bib keys stays in the honest witness-only list. DISCRIMINATION BY EXECUTION: dropping the hyphen from the prefix test gives 45 of 50 with the a-F1 versus a-F10 case red. NOT PAID DOWN: the 26 remaining rows are other agents ledgers to file into, and re-keying the four stems is an operator judgement since it changes keys already cited in notes.}
