  check    = {standing},
  note     = {kind=finding by=main. Sequitur vendored 2026-08-25, census identical at 926 phrases / 248 covered. Seven of the eighteen sites are the toolchain proper. synth_apex imported eliza and worked only because grammar_phrase_lattice mutated sys.path one line earlier. Named external consumer: cassian-observability, whose ordering constraint is that a root override without config vocabulary is the more dangerous half fix. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): Ⓘ ⟡memory-repo PACKAGING BLOCKER, HALF CLOSED 2026-08-25. The memory toolchain resolved imports two ways, both fatal to the PyPI-publishable target the operator set. FIRST, NOW FIXED: grammar_phrase_lattice climbed FOUR LEVELS OUT of the Claude-managed memory dir via sys.path.insert on a relative path into github/substrate/scratch/eliza, to reach Sequitur. Vendored as _vendor_sequitur.py, 522 lines, stdlib-only, unmodified but for a provenance header. Census identical after: 926 phrases, 248 of 316 covered, content matches, selftest 28 of 28. SECOND, STILL OPEN: sys.path.insert of HERE, measured 18 call sites across 16 files, of which SEVEN are the toolchain proper and the rest are probes that will not ship. That makes modules resolve by DIRECTORY ADJACENCY, which a package cannot do. ⚑ AND REMOVING THE FIRST EXPOSED A COUPLING THE SECOND WAS MASKING: synth_apex.py imported eliza and WORKED only because grammar_phrase_lattice, imported one line above, had already mutated sys.path as an import SIDE EFFECT. Nothing declared it. Reordering two lines would have broken the module, and it stayed invisible until the climb was removed and it raised ModuleNotFoundError. A dependency that works by accident of import order. ⚑⚑ THE CONSUMER IS NAMED AND EXTERNAL: cassian-observability vendored the seven scripts, then git reset hard when the closure was traced, and their operator ruled it into its own repo. Their framing on ordering is the design constraint — a root override without config vocabulary would still corrupt the concept space silently, so the path override alone is the MORE dangerous half fix. ⚑ MEASURING THIS WAS ITSELF THE ONE SPELLING ERROR: pycodemod --literal on the string found ONE hit, my own docstring, because it reads string literals and the statements are invisible to it. --calls insert found the eighteen.}
