}

@misc{cycle-detector-was-positional-and-wrong-both-ways,
  section  = {finding},
  rests-on = {modelling-the-antipattern-populated-the-dag},
  claim    = {A cycle detector keyed on emitted position under-reports the knot and over-reports it at the same time, and its output was published as a measurement.},
  check    = {selftest:python3,substrate/monolith_order_selftest.py},
  note     = {kind=finding by=claude. The test was whether a row's blocker appears LATER in the order. In a two-file knot the second member's blocker sits at an earlier index and is never flagged, so a three-file fixture returned one of three. Meanwhile a file merely STRANDED behind a cycle also carries a late blocker and was swept in, though cutting it frees nothing. Live it named twelve members, of which two carried no internal edge - gate_census at 741 findings and build_census at 389, an order of magnitude cheaper than the rest - and that anomaly is what exposed the defect rather than any case. The number was reported as a measurement before being checked. Repair - cycles() replays the emission so it cannot disagree with the pass that produced the order, and knot() uses mutual reachability because 'has an unplaced blocker' admits the stranded file and collapses to the same set. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): The first cycle detector tested whether a row's blocker appeared LATER in the emitted order, and that is wrong in both directions. Under-reports: in a two-file knot the second member's blocker sits at an EARLIER index, so it is never flagged - a three-file fixture returned one of three. Over-reports: a file merely STRANDED behind a cycle also fails the test while being on nobody's cut list. Live, it named twelve members, two of which (gate_census at 741 findings, build_census at 389) carried no internal edge at all - an order of magnitude cheaper than the rest, which is the anomaly that exposed the defect. I reported that twelve as a measurement. The repair is two readers - cycles() REPLAYS the emission (which rows had every blocker already out), so it cannot disagree with the pass that produced the order, and knot() uses MUTUAL REACHABILITY, since 'has an unplaced blocker' is too weak - a stranded file's blocker is itself unplaced, so that test returns the same set as cycles.}
}

@misc{the-knot-is-two-independent-knots,
