aged index is a fact about the INDEX, not about any module in it — the nine refusals are ban/public/rederive/sumtype/claims/discharge ratchets over AGDA and tool-census populations, none of which these five modules are in. I reported a repo-wide blocker as a per-module one, which is the holder-is-not-the-worker shape: an operation on the container reported as a fact about the contents. ⚑ WHAT REMAINS TRUE: the files are untracked, so a peer cannot FETCH them, and that was mtools' actual stated objection.}
