@misc{gate-F90-the-blind-inserts-are-one-imported-constant,
  section  = {finding},
  from     = {gate-F89-i-refiled-a-finding-i-had-declared-unpaired},
  claim    = {Over half the drain ranking's unattributed inserts are one imported constant, because the target resolver follows same-file bindings and not cross-module ones.},
  check    = {unwitnessed},
  note     = {kind=finding by=substrate. MEASURED: attr_reads wg_engine.LIBRARY reports 18 reads in wg_dispatch, wg_order and worklist_gate, and those three files hold 17 of the 33 opaque-target sites. LIBRARY binds os.path.join(ROOT, catalog, library) — resolvable, one module away. ⚑ insert_read.target_of reads literals in the Call, then falls back to path_binding.resolve_arg over derived, which file_derived_names computes for the SAME module only. An attribute read on an imported module has neither, so it returns UNKNOWN. ⚑⚑ This is a RANKING defect: unreadable's own docstring says a name scoring zero may hold an insert the reader could not read, so the worklist-gate family is systematically under-credited and the ranking is a floor. ⚑ 16 sites remain unexamined and may be other shapes — the 17 are measured, not a total. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): The 33 unattributed sys.path inserts in drain_leverage are not 33 distinct opacities. MEASURED: attr_reads wg_engine.LIBRARY reports 18 reads in 3 files — wg_dispatch, wg_order, worklist_gate — and those three hold 17 of the 33 reported opaque-target sites. wg_engine.LIBRARY binds os.path.join(ROOT, catalog, library), a fully resolvable directory one module away. ⚑ READ THE BINDING: insert_read.target_of reads string literals inside the Call first, then falls back to path_binding.resolve_arg over derived, which file_derived_names computes for THE SAME MODULE ONLY. An insert whose target is an attribute read on an IMPORTED module has no literal in the call and no same-file binding, so it returns UNKNOWN. The reader follows intra-file bindings and not cross-module ones. ⚑⚑ THE CONSEQUENCE IS A RANKING DEFECT, NOT MERELY A GAP, AND unreadable's OWN DOCSTRING STATES IT: a name scoring zero retired inserts may simply hold one this reader could not read. So the drain ranking that answers what-to-drain-first is a FLOOR, and the three worklist-gate-family files are systematically under-credited — a drain of that family would retire inserts the ranking cannot see. ⚑ NOT ALL 33: 16 remain unexamined and may be other shapes. Reporting the 17 measured, not a total.}
}

