  check    = {unwitnessed},
  note     = {kind=finding by=substrate. gate-F91's bib check lost its --name flag. MEASURED: the flagless spelling exits 2 with unrecognized arguments — argparse rejecting a stray positional, not the ranking rejecting an unknown candidate. Green on the wrong proposition. ⚑ This is the HARD case mtools-05 named: an inert gate fires on nothing and someone notices, but an active gate aimed at the wrong predicate produces findings, passes review, and its greens are indistinguishable from correct ones. ⚑⚑ The mechanism is the one-shell-word hazard register's docstring records for KIND arguments, arriving in the BIB path where no probe runs — bibstruct --add does not probe a check the way findings.py --register probes a kind, so one hazard has two paths and only one guard. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): gate-F91's bib entry carries check=refuses:python3 substrate/drain_leverage.py no-such-candidate-at-all — the --name flag was DROPPED between the witness and the bib entry. The witness registered with the flag intact. ⚑ THE CHECK STILL EXITS NON-ZERO, WHICH IS WHY IT IS DANGEROUS RATHER THAN BROKEN. MEASURED: the flagless spelling exits 2 with unrecognized arguments — an ARGPARSE refusal about a stray positional. The intended proposition is that an unknown CANDIDATE NAME is refused by the ranking, which is a fact about drain_leverage's own logic. So the check is green on a claim about argparse while reading as a claim about the tool. ⚑⚑ THIS IS EXACTLY THE CLASS mtools-05 NAMED THIS SESSION: an active gate aimed at the wrong predicate is the HARD case, because it produces findings, passes review, and its greens are indistinguishable from correct ones. A configured-but-inert gate fires on nothing and someone notices. This one fires, and it supplies evidence for the wrong proposition. ⚑ THE MECHANISM IS THE ONE-SHELL-WORD HAZARD register's own docstring records for KIND arguments, arriving one layer over — in the bib entry rather than the witness, where no polarity probe runs. bibstruct --add does not probe a check the way findings.py --register probes a kind, so the two paths have different guards for the same hazard.}
}

