mitting 'see .claude/skills/struct-tools/SKILL.md' at hook_no_chaining:407 and hook_structural_query:343, both arg role - text a refused party receives - pointing at a substrate-local directory of ten skills. ⚑ THE THIRD IS THE WORST BECAUSE THE SAME REFUSAL ALREADY ANTICIPATED THE FAILURE MODE FOR THE TOOL AND NOT FOR THE SKILL: hook_structural_query offers 'use the harness Read' when pycodemod is absent, in the same message that emits a skill path with no fallback. ⚑⚑ AND THE FAILURE IS SILENT, which is why it outranks an unresolvable import. An import fails loudly at import time. A dangling successor fails as advice a reader cannot act on, so the gate looks complete and nothing errors. ⚑ I DID NOT FIND THIS MYSELF - mtools asked whether its own emitted skill path violated the article substrate had just filed, and substrate's copy surfaced only because the question was put. An article's author is not the party best placed to find its violations in their own tree.}
