  note     = {kind=selftest by=substrate. Lands the gate-G49 repair and answers SB-A10 from mtools constitution census, where the question had been posed as name-a-reachable-successor versus name-none. The third option is to inline the portable part and drop the coordinate. MEASURED before editing. mdstruct --budget over the target reports 21618 of 40681 bytes in a generated mode census plus a tools roster and an artifact-to-tool table, so the pointer named a ROSTER a consumer cannot use, while the one fully portable paragraph was the part the refusal omitted. Each hook inlines the rule that fits IT. no_chaining takes the permission argument read verbatim from SKILL.md 715-720, structural_query takes the blind-spot cost argument, and copying either into the other would be a second spelling of a different rule. Suites 50 to 53 and 59 to 62. The refusal text was UNPINNED beforehand and both suites passed unchanged after the edit, which is the mode-B signal that nothing guarded the shared product. Cases assert both directions. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): The gate-G49 repair LANDED in both vendored hooks. Each refusal used to close on see .claude/skills/struct-tools/SKILL.md, a path resolving only in substrate while both files are vendored by cassian as the nc and sq claim families. Measured against the target with mdstruct --budget. 21618 of 40681 bytes are a GENERATED mode census plus a tools roster and an artifact-to-tool table, so a consumer holding the hook has neither the tools nor the census and the pointer bought them nothing. Each hook now inlines ITS OWN portable rule rather than the one belonging to its sibling. hook_no_chaining carries the permission argument that a chain cannot be approved in a way that sticks, verified verbatim at SKILL.md lines 715-720 and containing nothing substrate-specific. hook_structural_query carries the cost argument that a regex over a structured artifact reports its own blind spots as facts about the subject. Copying one into the other would have been a second spelling of a different rule. Suites 50 to 53 and 59 to 62, and the refusal text was UNPINNED before this. Nothing asserted the pointer and nothing would have caught its loss, which is the mode-B hazard on shared machinery. Both directions are cased because demanding the rule passes with a dead pointer still appended, and forbidding the pointer passes if the rule were dropped.}
