  claim    = {The spelling-pair matcher is drained to substrate/finding_restem.py at 19 of 19, with the trailing-hyphen boundary asserted by CONSEQUENCE -- a fixture where dropping it both marries two unrelated findings and destroys the genuine pair. The drain has since COMPLETED -- the module was promoted to mikemol.ledger.finding_restem and the local twin deleted (W40, 2026-09-26); this witness holds while it stays deleted.},
  check    = {refuses:.venv/bin/python,-c,import substrate.finding_restem},
  note     = {kind=selftest by=substrate. Third unit after finding_kinds and finding_resolve, and it is the reader that saved the pairing census from its own defect. pairing reported 20 witness-only and 10 bib-only rows where four of each were the same four findings under two spellings, counted twice on opposite sides of one report, so reading thirty rows as thirty findings would have filed four duplicate bib entries and four duplicate witnesses -- census-keyed-on-one-spelling occurring inside the census built to detect that class. THE HYPHEN IS CASED BY CONSEQUENCE RATHER THAN BY READING THE PATTERN. The fixture holds aa-F1 beside aa-F10-a-completely-different-one, so a matcher without the boundary fails in two ways at once and a case inspecting the regex would pass on a matcher that holds the hyphen and misuses it. THE ARITHMETIC IS PINNED AS AN INEQUALITY. raw rows exceed true drift whenever a pair exists and the difference equals the pair count, because pinning the current 28 versus 24 would expire the moment either population moves, which is gate-G40's reach-floor defect. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): Third drain unit landed as substrate/finding_restem.py, 19 of 19 with four differential cases. This is the reader that saved the pairing census from itself -- pairing reported 20 witness-only and 10 bib-only where four of each were THE SAME four findings under two spellings, so a naive paydown of thirty rows would have filed four duplicate bib entries and four duplicate witnesses, growing the drift through the instrument built to shrink it. THE HYPHEN CASE IS ASSERTED BY CONSEQUENCE RATHER THAN BY INSPECTING THE PATTERN. The fixture carries aa-F1 and aa-F10-a-completely-different-one, so a matcher dropping the boundary marries two unrelated findings AND loses the genuine pair, failing in two ways at once. A case that read the regex would pass on a matcher holding the hyphen and using it wrongly. AND THE DOUBLE-COUNT IS PINNED AS AN INEQUALITY rather than as a number -- raw rows must exceed true drift whenever a pair exists, and the difference must equal the pair count. Pinning todays 28 versus 24 would expire the moment either population moves, which is the reach-floor-as-majority-claim defect from gate-G40.}
