  check    = {unwitnessed},
  note     = {kind=unwitnessed by=substrate. Found by taking cassian-observability-da's offered class seriously rather than acknowledging it. Their instance was a tofu count-gate defaulted false, crossed by an attended apply passing -var on the command line, the value dying with the shell -- a bare plan then proposed 13 destroys including the live RBE executor, and their check found a second independent instance on its first run. SUBSTRATE HAS NO TERRAFORM SURFACE, find returns zero .tf files, so that spelling cannot arise and reporting only that would have been a fact about the spelling rather than the class. THE GENERAL SHAPE IS LIVE. git diff on .claude/settings.json shows the whole env block arming STRUCT_HOOK_BLOCK, NOCHAIN_HOOK_BLOCK, PYCHECK_HOOK_BLOCK and SHELLCHECK_HOOK_BLOCK, plus every PreToolUse registration, sitting uncommitted. hook_fire_probe --report reads 12 of 12 arms ok with denies where expected, so the hooks are demonstrably live. The vector differs -- an untracked working-tree edit rather than a command-line var -- and the two-sided switch and the silent side-flip are identical. COMPOUNDS gate-G58 because a peer invoking these hooks by path gets an arming configuration in no commit. Substrate does get one thing right that they did not. blocking_vars DERIVES the arming from settings.json rather than hardcoding it, its docstring naming the reason as refusing to certify a gate against a copy of its own configuration. NOT REPAIRED. committing a permissions and hooks config is the operator call. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): cassian-observability-da offered a class from their tofu cutover -- gate it false so a bare apply cannot create it, run the attended apply with a command-line var, and the value dies with the shell, leaving the declaration inverted while touching no artifact. Their bare plan proposed 13 destroys including the live RBE executor. SUBSTRATE HAS NO TERRAFORM SURFACE. find over the tree returns zero .tf files, so that spelling cannot arise. BUT THE GENERAL SHAPE IS LIVE HERE AND I FOUND IT BY TAKING THE OFFER SERIOUSLY. git diff on .claude/settings.json shows the ENTIRE hook installation is uncommitted -- the env block arming all four hooks and the whole PreToolUse registration for structural_query, no_chaining, shellcheck and pycheck. HEAD carries neither block. So the LIVE state is four hooks armed and denying, confirmed by hook_fire_probe --report reading 12 of 12 arms ok with deny where deny is expected, while the DECLARED state in HEAD is that no hooks exist at all. Same two-sided switch and same silent side-flip as theirs, with an untracked working-tree edit as the vector instead of a command-line var. IT COMPOUNDS gate-G58. peers invoking substrate hooks by path get files whose arming configuration is in no commit either. NOT REPAIRED HERE. committing a permissions and hooks configuration is the operator call, not mine, and staging it would be deciding it.}
}

@misc{gate-G65-the-kind-parser-is-drained,
  section  = {finding},
  claim    = {The kind parser is drained to substrate/finding_kindspec.py at 33 of 33, carrying the four-kind refusal menu with its ORDER asserted -- listing standing first would pass a presence check while restoring the defect that made it the default. The drain has since COMPLETED -- the module was promoted to mikemol.ledger.finding_kindspec (witness_check and witness_run import it there) and the local twin deleted (W40, 2026-09-26); this witness holds while it stays deleted.},
