insert is DELIBERATE and reasoned in a comment directly above it -- it self-supplies the repo root so an ADOPTING checkout can resolve substrate.ratchet_flags, and it uses absolute rather than resolve specifically because resolve follows symlinks and would derive SUBSTRATE root in a symlinked adopter. So the code is defensible and SB-L2 as I wrote it is too absolute. The article is wrong, not the export. AND IT IS THE SAME FILE AS SB-13, which I retracted after a peer measured an import two of my instruments missed. Same file, same class, third miss, and my own inlined hook rule caught the fourth attempt when I reached for sed.}
