  note     = {kind=finding by=substrate-session. Both instruments are honest and answer different questions — commit_refusal asks what would refuse THIS staged index and reports 29 UNMEASURABLE, gate_status runs the gates and reports verdicts. Eight of gate_status's reds are gates commit_refusal cannot measure and so does not count — selftest roster current, tool selftests, feature coverage, carrier locality, snapshot guard, type gate mypy, stub authority, scratch-independence. commit_refusal PRINTS 29 UNMEASURABLE — no verdict, NOT clean, directly beside the 8, and I quoted the 8 every tick and read past the other. A third outcome that is load-bearing, emitted by the tool, treated by its reader as absence. THE UNMEASURED BAND HOLDS THE LARGEST FIGURE IN THE TREE — type gate reports 1144 NEW type errors, invisible in every refusal summary I have reported. ⚑ AND IT CONFIRMS gate-G134 AGAINST A THIRD INSTRUMENT — check_scratch_independence enumerates 12 live scratch references in promoted projects, 7 runtime, every one under jea/metalanguage and none under substrate/, so the drained modules are absent from the red population as well as the refusing one. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): I have quoted 8 gates WOULD REFUSE every tick from commit_refusal. gate_status over the same tree reads 18 red of 37. Both are honest and they answer different questions — commit_refusal asks what would refuse THIS staged index and reports 29 as UNMEASURABLE, while gate_status runs the gates and reports their actual verdicts. THE DISAGREEMENT IS ENTIRELY IN THE UNMEASURABLE BAND. Eight of gate_status's reds are gates commit_refusal cannot measure and therefore does not count — selftest roster current, tool selftests, feature coverage, carrier locality, snapshot guard, type gate (mypy), stub authority, scratch-independence. commit_refusal SAYS SO IN ITS OWN OUTPUT, printing 29 UNMEASURABLE — no verdict, NOT clean, and I read past that line every tick while quoting the 8 beside it. A third outcome that is load-bearing, printed by the tool, and treated by its reader as absence. THE UNMEASURED BAND CONTAINS A LARGE FIGURE — type gate reports 1144 NEW type errors. That is not visible anywhere in the refusal summary I have been reporting, and it is the largest single quantity in the tree's gate surface. ⚑ AND IT CONFIRMS gate-G134 AGAINST A THIRD INSTRUMENT RATHER THAN REFUTING IT. check_scratch_independence enumerates 12 live scratch references in promoted projects, 7 runtime, and EVERY ONE is under jea/metalanguage. None under substrate/. So the drained modules are absent from the red population as well as from the refusing population, and the atomic-commit reading holds.}
