agreement and is not one — file_header's own docstring says IT READS COMMENTS NOT STRINGS AND ONLY THE HEAD OF THE FILE, because scanning the whole file would count a header quoted inside a docstring, so a module documenting the convention would read as conforming to it. A literal-STRING search cannot see a COMMENT prefix. I then opened gate_census.py expecting a conforming example and it has no header either, being one of the 82 NEITHER. THE AUTHORITY WAS THE CONSTANT ALL ALONG — SPDX_PREFIX is # SPDX-License-Identifier: and COPYRIGHT_PREFIX is # Copyright, read from file_header directly after two failed searches. ⚑ AND file_header HAS NO PER-FILE LISTING MODE. Its bare run is a census with tree totals and no way to name WHICH files conform, so finding a conforming example is not a question the tool answers. That is a missing mode and therefore work, recorded rather than routed around.}
