ds the import and its use in ONE write — adding the import alone is refused as F401 unused, and adding the use alone is refused as F821 undefined. Both directions measured. The file is 218 lines so a whole rewrite is the admissible form, and that is a turn of its own rather than the tail of this one. ⚑⚑ AND THE FILE'S OWN DOCSTRING ALREADY RETRACTED THE READING I RE-DERIVED AS NEW LAST TICK. gate-F96 records that substrate told a peer it has NO licence-header population citing pycodemod --literal returning zero, then corrected it to zero-under-substrate, and that BOTH readings are void because --literal searches STRING CONSTANTS while a licence header is a COMMENT. I hit that same wall in gate-G145 and filed it as a fresh discovery. The retraction was sitting in the docstring of the file I was measuring. ⚑ AND MY HEADER SPELLING IS WRONG. This file carries # Copyright (c) 2026 Mike Mol and I wrote # Copyright substrate contributors into scan_root — both satisfy the COPYRIGHT_PREFIX test so the census cannot see the difference, which is a second thing that reader does not distinguish.}
