  check    = {unwitnessed},
  note     = {kind=finding by=substrate-session reported-by=cassian-observability. They reported mdstruct unrunnable through a symlink — abspath does not resolve symlinks so ROOT becomes the CALLER's tree, the sys.path insert points at a directory with no climode, and the bare import dies. REPRODUCED AND EXACT AT THE EXACT LINE NUMBERS, with one correction — the file is scratch/mdstruct.py not scripts/. scripts/mdstruct.py does not exist here and their cited 139, 238, 239 are the right lines of the scratch file, so this is a reference to a moved artifact rather than a wrong reading. AND IT IS gate-F56 FROM OUTSIDE — module_importers substrate.climode reports 13 BARE sites beside 4 dotted and states the general case itself, that a bare site resolves only under a sys.path insert and FAILS for an adopter importing the installed wheel. mdstruct is one of fourteen consumers already recorded blocked, and cassian is the first party to hit it from the consumer side rather than the census side. THEIR SIBLING COMPARISON IS THE LOAD-BEARING EVIDENCE — bibstruct.py runs through the identical symlink because it was converted to a shim over the substrate package, so the symlink is not the defect. A differential control across a converted and an unconverted file is what separates a tool defect from an environment one. THE REPAIR IS BLOCKED — scratch/mdstruct.py carries 1195 findings across 60 rules, so both remedies they offer are edits to a refused file. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): cassian reported scripts/mdstruct.py unrunnable through a symlink — abspath does not resolve symlinks, so ROOT becomes the CALLER's tree, the sys.path insert points at a directory with no climode, and the bare-name import dies. REPRODUCED THE DIAGNOSIS AND IT IS EXACT AT THE EXACT LINE NUMBERS, with one correction — THE FILE IS scratch/mdstruct.py NOT scripts/. scripts/mdstruct.py does not exist here, and their cited 139, 238 and 239 are the right lines of the scratch file. A path that names a real defect at real line numbers in a directory the tool does not live in is the reference-to-a-moved-artifact shape rather than a wrong reading. AND IT IS NOT AN mdstruct DEFECT — IT IS gate-F56 ARRIVING FROM OUTSIDE. module_importers substrate.climode reports 13 BARE sites beside 4 dotted and states the general case in its own output — a bare site names the module by its leaf alone, resolves only under a sys.path insert, and FAILS for an adopter importing the installed wheel. mdstruct is one of fourteen consumers already recorded as blocked, and cassian is the first party to hit it from the consumer side rather than the census side. THEIR SIBLING COMPARISON IS THE LOAD-BEARING EVIDENCE — bibstruct.py runs through the identical symlink because it was converted to a shim over the substrate package, so the symlink is not the defect. That is a differential control against a converted and an unconverted file, which is exactly what separates a tool defect from an environment one. THE REPAIR IS BLOCKED. scratch/mdstruct.py carries 1195 findings across 60 rules, so neither remedy they offer can land — the dotted import and the realpath fix are both edits to a refused file. gate-F56's own text says the population is uniform and this confirms it from a new direction.}
