  note     = {kind=finding by=substrate-session. gate-G150 hypothesised that runnable-through-a-symlink IS package-reachability and the wanted check might be a reading of an existing census. TESTED AND THE READER EXISTED, UNBOUND — syspath_census already had census, render, total_sites, owning_files and a show parameter naming files, with NO dispatch, so the only route was an inline script the no-chaining hook correctly refuses. SECOND BUILT-THEN-UNBOUND READER IN THREE TICKS after file_header.missing. MEASURED ONCE BOUND — 486 mutations across 308 files, scratch at 152 sites in 109 files, metalanguage 78, scripts 56, eliza 47. An insert computed from __file__ makes the CALLER's directory importable when abspath does not resolve the link, so every one of those files can fail as mdstruct did for cassian. A FLOOR NOT A VERDICT, WHICH THE READER STATES — 33 sites in 17 files are <unresolved> because the argument is computed and has no static target, so a tool can carry the hazard and read as unresolved rather than exposed. ⚑ THE HYPOTHESIS HOLDS IN THE DIRECTION THAT MATTERS — a tool with NO insert cannot fail this way, which is why bibstruct runs through the symlink after conversion to a package shim. The static census answers the safe half exactly and bounds the unsafe half, so no cross-repo probe is needed to IDENTIFY candidates, only to confirm one. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): gate-G150 hypothesised that runnable-through-a-symlink IS package-reachability and that the check cassian wants might be a reading of an existing census rather than a new probe. TESTED IT AND THE READER EXISTED, UNBOUND. substrate/syspath_census.py already had census, render, total_sites, owning_files and a show parameter that names files — and NO DISPATCH, so the only way to ask was an inline script, which the no-chaining hook correctly refuses because a judgement made in a turn evaporates with it. SECOND BUILT-THEN-UNBOUND READER IN THREE TICKS after file_header.missing. MEASURED ONCE BOUND — 486 sys.path mutations across 308 files, led by scratch at 152 sites in 109 files, metalanguage at 78, scripts at 56, eliza at 47. That is the symlink-hazard population statically enumerated, because an insert computed from __file__ makes the CALLER's directory importable rather than the tool's when abspath does not resolve the link. Every one of those files can fail the way mdstruct failed for cassian. AND IT IS A FLOOR RATHER THAN A VERDICT, WHICH THE READER SAYS ITSELF — 33 sites in 17 files report as <unresolved> because the insert argument is computed and has no statically knowable target, so a tool can carry the hazard and be reported as unresolved rather than as exposed. ⚑ THE HYPOTHESIS HOLDS IN THE DIRECTION THAT MATTERS. A tool with NO insert cannot fail this way, which is why bibstruct runs through the symlink after its conversion to a package shim. So the static census answers the safe half exactly and bounds the unsafe half, and no cross-repo probe is needed to identify candidates — only to confirm one.}
}

