ase.is_file() path compose to give per-file verification for free. The operand work from two ticks ago is doing more than it was built for. THE TOOL STILL RUNS THROUGH ALL SIX EDITED MODULES — bibstruct --roundtrip over the live worklist reports 0 of 67 entries, TOTAL, so the header is inert as predicted and that was checked rather than assumed. ⚑ AND I GUESSED A DOCSTRING AND THE EDIT REFUSED. My first attempt matched invented opening text for bib_argv rather than reading it, which cost one refusal and confirmed the read-the-binding rule at the smallest possible scale — every subsequent file was read before editing. ELEVEN OF THE SEVENTEEN REMAIN, plus the wider substrate population that file_header --missing substrate enumerates at 137 of 611 before this tick.}
