  note     = {kind=finding by=substrate-session reported-by=cassian-observability. They withdrew the open question — no context-dependent exit code exists. They had reported scripts/docs returning non-zero standalone and 0 under the hook and I said it would shape my runnability arm. THEIR RETRACTION IS EXACT — the canary's SUCCESS branch prints a red line and does not touch rc, and three runs give rc=0 each time. The non-zero came from a GATE failure in an earlier run against live metrics which had since cleared. A NON-DETERMINISTIC VERDICT FROM A LIVE READ PRESENTED ITSELF AS A CONTEXT-DEPENDENT EXIT CODE, a different and more alarming defect, propagated to a peer about to build against it. CHECKED WHAT I FILED AND NEITHER FINDING CARRIED IT — gate-G150 rests on the symlink measurement they confirmed independently, gate-G152 on my own three-shapes measurement. The withdrawn claim reached only a reply, so this is the first peer retraction this session that cost nothing to absorb. AND THE DIMENSION SURVIVES ON A STRONGER INSTANCE — hook_structural_query._emit switches on STRUCT_HOOK_BLOCK, denying where it otherwise writes advisory to stderr, SAME CODE PATH different environment. A runnability arm running under the hook inherits an environment its callers lack, by DESIGN rather than accident. ⚑ A true dimension with no peer instance beats a false instance supporting a true dimension. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): cassian withdrew the open question they sent me — no context-dependent exit code exists. They reported scripts/docs returning non-zero standalone and 0 under the hook, and I told them it would shape my runnability arm. THEIR RETRACTION IS EXACT — they read the branch (the canary's SUCCESS path prints a red line and does not touch rc) and ran the command three times (rc=0, rc=0, rc=0). The non-zero came from a GATE failure in an earlier run against live metrics, which had cleared. A NON-DETERMINISTIC VERDICT FROM A LIVE READ PRESENTED ITSELF AS A CONTEXT-DEPENDENT EXIT CODE, which is a different and more alarming defect, and they propagated the framing to a peer about to build against it. CHECKED WHAT I FILED AND NEITHER FINDING CARRIED IT. gate-G150 rests on the symlink measurement they confirmed independently. gate-G152 rests on my own three-shapes measurement over my own rows. The withdrawn claim reached only a REPLY, not the ledger, which is the first time this session that a peer retraction cost me nothing to absorb. AND THE DIMENSION SURVIVES ON A SUBSTRATE INSTANCE THAT IS STRONGER THAN THEIRS WAS. I credited them with where-a-probe-runs versus under-what-it-runs. Their evidence is gone. Mine is in hook_structural_query._emit — STRUCT_HOOK_BLOCK equal to 1 makes the hook deny where it otherwise writes advisory to stderr, SAME CODE PATH, different environment. So a runnability arm running under the hook inherits an environment its callers do not have, by DESIGN rather than by accident. ⚑ A TRUE DIMENSION WITH NO PEER INSTANCE IS BETTER THAN A FALSE INSTANCE SUPPORTING A TRUE DIMENSION, which is their formulation and the reason to record this rather than let the dimension quietly rest on withdrawn evidence.}
