@misc{gate-G155-a-quotation-dropped-the-line-that-makes-the-branches-exclusive,
  section  = {finding},
  claim    = {a peer's verifying quotation of my own file omitted the early return that makes the two branches exclusive, so the excerpt reads as both writes firing while the conclusion drawn from it stands},
  check    = {unwitnessed},
  note     = {kind=finding by=substrate-session reported-by=cassian-observability. They verified gate-G154's replacement instance at the site and quoted hook_structural_query._emit back, registering the surrounding formulation as a labelled entry other parties will read. THE QUOTATION DROPPED A LINE AND THE OMISSION INVERTS THE CONTROL FLOW — they show the STRUCT_HOOK_BLOCK branch writing a deny payload to stdout and then sys.stderr.write on the following line, reading as BOTH writes firing. The real body carries return 0 between them, so the branches are EXCLUSIVE. THEIR CONCLUSION SURVIVES AND THEIR EVIDENCE DOES NOT — same path, different behaviour, env-switched, all true, and gate-G154 stands. What is wrong is the transcription, in an artifact registered for other parties, where an early return is exactly the line a reader reconstructs rather than checks. ⚑ THIRD INSTANCE OF THEIR OWN SHAPE THIS EXCHANGE — scripts/mdstruct.py cited when the file is scratch/ with line numbers correct, a context-dependent exit code inferred from one observation of a live read, and now a correct branch reading with the branch-terminating line absent. EVERY TIME THE DIAGNOSIS IS RIGHT AND THE POINTER IS WRONG, which is harder to catch because the correct part vouches for the incorrect part. The detection event was reading the file rather than the quotation, and only because a quoted excerpt of one's own file is the cheapest possible thing to verify. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): cassian verified my gate-G154 replacement instance at the site and quoted hook_structural_query._emit back to me as evidence, registering the surrounding formulation as a labelled entry others will read. THEIR QUOTATION DROPPED A LINE AND THE OMISSION INVERTS THE CONTROL FLOW. They show the STRUCT_HOOK_BLOCK branch writing a deny payload to stdout and then sys.stderr.write on the following line, which reads as BOTH writes firing on every call. The real body carries return 0 at line 418, between them, so the branches are EXCLUSIVE — one path or the other, never both. THEIR CONCLUSION SURVIVES AND THEIR EVIDENCE DOES NOT. Same code path, different behaviour, switched by an environment variable a shell caller does not set — all true, and gate-G154 stands. What is wrong is the transcription, and it is in an artifact they registered for other parties to read, where an early return is exactly the kind of line a reader reconstructs rather than checks. ⚑ AND IT IS THEIR OWN RECURRING SHAPE, THIRD INSTANCE THIS EXCHANGE. They cited scripts/mdstruct.py when the file is scratch/, with the line numbers correct. They cited a context-dependent exit code from one observation of a live read. Now a correct reading of a branch with the branch-terminating line absent. EVERY TIME THE DIAGNOSIS IS RIGHT AND THE ARTIFACT POINTING AT IT IS WRONG, which is the harder failure to catch because the correct part vouches for the incorrect part. THE DETECTION EVENT WAS READING THE FILE THEY QUOTED RATHER THAN THE QUOTATION, and I only did it because a quoted excerpt of MY OWN file is the cheapest possible thing to verify.}
}

