@misc{gate-G159-i-called-a-designed-library-an-orphan-by-running-it-directly,
  section  = {finding},
  claim    = {a library correctly reached through its sibling's dispatch was read as a third built-then-unbound orphan because two genuine instances had made the shape a lens},
  check    = {unwitnessed},
  note     = {kind=finding by=substrate-session. I ran drain_blockers.py bare, got silence, and concluded it was a third unbound reader after file_header.missing and syspath_census — sharper, I reasoned, because drain_plan's output advertises --blockers while the tool appears unreachable. READ THE BINDING AND IT INVERTS — drain_plan.main handles --blockers and calls drain_blockers.render directly. THE MODE IS BOUND. drain_blockers is a LIBRARY BY DESIGN reached through its sibling's dispatch, and the advertisement is correct rather than dangling since it names a mode of the tool a caller is already running. SO SILENCE ON A BARE RUN HAS AT LEAST FOUR CAUSES HERE — a library that SHOULD have a CLI and lacks one (two real instances, both repaired), a library that correctly has none because a sibling dispatches it (this), a tool whose bare run IS its usage, and a tool that failed to start. My earlier triple of never-existed, vanished, and exists-with-no-reader was missing the member where NO READER IS THE RIGHT ANSWER. ⚑ THE PATTERN-MATCH IS WHAT DID IT — two genuine instances in three ticks made the third read as confirmation, and the advertisement made it read as aggravated. A shape confirmed twice becomes a lens, and the candidate was checked against the lens rather than against the binding. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): I ran substrate/drain_blockers.py bare, got silence, and concluded it was a THIRD built-then-unbound reader after file_header.missing and syspath_census — sharper than either, I reasoned, because drain_plan's own output advertises --blockers as the next step while the tool appears unreachable. READ THE BINDING AND THE INFERENCE INVERTS. drain_plan.main line 92 handles --blockers and calls drain_blockers.render(rows, top, own) directly. THE MODE IS BOUND. drain_blockers is a LIBRARY BY DESIGN, reached through its sibling's dispatch, and the advertisement in drain_plan's output is correct rather than dangling — it names the mode of the tool a caller is already running. SO SILENCE ON A BARE RUN HAS AT LEAST FOUR CAUSES IN THIS TREE, not the three I had. A library with no CLI that SHOULD have one (file_header.missing, syspath_census — both real, both repaired). A library with no CLI that correctly has none because a sibling dispatches it (this). A tool whose bare run is its usage. And a tool that failed to start. My census-green triple from gate-G157's reply — never existed, vanished, exists with no reader — was missing the member where NO READER IS THE RIGHT ANSWER. ⚑ AND THE PATTERN-MATCH IS WHAT DID IT. Two genuine instances in three ticks made the third read as confirmation, and the ADVERTISEMENT made it read as an aggravated case. A shape confirmed twice becomes a lens, and the third candidate was checked against the lens rather than against the binding. That is the architecture-shaped-findings-get-built-against class arriving in my own reading rather than in a peer's report.}
}

