@misc{gate-G266-regenerating-the-roster-inverts-its-own-witness,
  section  = {finding},
  from     = {gate-G265-selftest-mk-is-stale-and-this-arc-own-suites-would-not-run},
  claim    = {A finding witnessed by a command that reads mutable state has its witness inverted by its own repair, so the ledger reports the finding as gone at exactly the moment the work lands and the record of why it was filed survives only in the note.},
  check    = {selftest:python3,-m,substrate.selftest_mk,--check},
  note     = {kind=selftest by=substrate. The witness: python3 -m substrate.selftest_mk regenerated 437 suites and --check now exits 0 where gate-G265 filed refuses: on it exiting 1 one tick earlier. suite_gap_report confirms tree_root and borrowed_root hold suites. The regeneration was provably additive because check reports declared-but-not-discovered as minus rows and the stale output carried none. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): Selftest.mk regenerated: 437 suites declared, --check now exits 0 silently, and suite_gap_report confirms tree_root and borrowed_root are not among the 29 modules lacking a suite. The precondition was read rather than assumed — check reports BOTH directions with a minus row for declared-but-not-discovered, and the stale output carried only plus rows, so the regeneration was provably additive and no declared suite could be lost. And the repair INVERTS gate-G265's own witness: that finding was filed refuses: on this exact command one tick ago because it exited 1, and it now exits 0, so the witness asserts the finding is gone the moment the finding is fixed. A witness whose command reads mutable state cannot hold a stable polarity across its own repair — the rule this session carries, arriving on a witness I registered myself.}
}

@misc{gate-G267-module-trim-repaired-and-the-repair-moved-the-failure-to-an-honest-one,
