  note     = {kind=unwitnessed by=momentum. substrate/md_hkey.agree folds smart typography and asks exactly the raw-versus-rendered question gate-G297 names, and attr_reads md_hkey.agree reports 16 reads in 1 of 1593 files — every one inside md_hkey_selftest. Zero production callers while md_spans._anchors kept calling md_ast.anchor_key, which strips markup and cannot un-rewrite a codepoint. ⚑ THE DOCSTRING SAYS THE WORDS — normalise a heading so raw source and rendered agree — so the seam was named, solved and never connected. ⚑⚑ OPERATOR RULED LEAVE IT UNWIRED: the module is slated for deletion under the mdstruct purge, so repairing it would be a third copy of one fix, and md_hkey goes upstream to mtools as cargo rather than landing here as a repair. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): substrate/md_hkey.agree folds smart typography and answers the raw-versus-rendered heading question that gate-G297 is about, and attr_reads finds 16 reads of it ALL inside its own suite with zero production callers — so the repair for a live defect existed, tested, in the same tree as the defect, reachable by nothing, while md_spans._anchors kept calling the reader that cannot un-rewrite a codepoint}
