  check    = {standing},
  note     = {kind=finding by=momentum. MEASURED — substrate/agda_census_run.py stopped reaching gen_build_makefiles (reach-back 42 names to 41, that name gone entirely, adopter-usable 800 to 801, intake 813 to 814) and intake_manifest --names dropped it from SOLE 2 to 1. But adopter_import still reports it ModuleNotFoundError on agda_lex, reached through substrate.agda_tree_state. Both instruments are correct and answer different questions — reading the manifest drop as adopter-importable would have banked a false green. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): intake_manifest reads module-scope reach while adopter_import reads transitive runtime import, so paying a module's OWN unpackaged name drops it from the SOLE list while it stays unimportable behind a packaged sibling that still reaches one — the manifest drop is not a release}
}

@misc{gate-G353,
  section  = {finding},
  claim    = {A memoised reader has two return paths and a copy-guard arm reaches only the warm one, so asserting non-identity after both calls are cached passes against a cache-MISS return that leaks its stored object},
