  note     = {kind=finding by=momentum. MEASURED — the arm asserted two gates over private_ratchet_baseline.txt, the package gate and its scripts-era origin. gate_population --gates lists eighteen gates with no check_private_ratchet.py and tool_population --find private finds no such file, so the origin is gone and the count is one. A literal census found a third namer that is not a gate at all, ratchet_key.SCHEMA, which carries the filename as data. Rendering the table then showed the same two-gates-over-one-ledger condition LIVE on public_ratchet_baseline.txt, held by scripts/check_public_ratchet.py and substrate/public_gate.py at equal key counts, so both states are now pinned by their own arms and each goes red when its migration moves. AND THE MODULE HAD NO CLI — render and degraded were public and reachable only by import, so a bare run printed nothing, which is indistinguishable from a clean tree in a module whose subject is baselines nobody looks at. 15/16 to 17/17. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): baseline_health_selftest asserted that the migrated private gate and its scripts-era origin share one baseline, expecting exactly two rows over private_ratchet_baseline.txt. It read 15/16 because THE MIGRATION COMPLETED. MEASURED — gate_population --gates lists eighteen gates and no check_private_ratchet.py, and tool_population --find private finds no such file, so the origin is gone and one gate owns that ledger. A tracker of a transition MUST fail when the transition lands, the same shape as the --dropped arm that went red the day its mode bound, so the arm now asserts the finished state and still fails if a second gate reappears. AND A LITERAL CENSUS FOUND A THIRD NAMER THAT IS NOT A GATE — ratchet_key.SCHEMA carries the filename as DATA, which is why gate_population correctly does not count it. ⚑⚑ THE CONDITION DID NOT DISAPPEAR, IT MOVED: rendering the table showed public_ratchet_baseline.txt carrying TWO rows, scripts/check_public_ratchet.py and substrate/public_gate.py at the same key count, so the public migration is the live instance and is now pinned by its own arm. ⚑ AND THE MODULE HAD NO CLI — render and degraded were public and reachable only by import, so running it bare printed nothing, indistinguishable from a clean tree. Added the mode to the owning reader. 15/16 to 17/17.}
